  // tension peaks at the end of the range rather than at the bottom, so the
  // spinal and joint loading that makes a barbell squat or row a lower-back
  // risk is not the same movement. Where the risk IS the position rather than
  // the load (upright row for shoulders, good morning for the lower back), it
  // is kept.
